  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="sp-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h2">
    <div class="sp-faq-inner">
      <p class="sp-section-label">Questions</p>
      <h2 class="sp-section-h2" id="faq-h2">CMU Block Installation FAQ<br><em>Answered Honestly</em></h2>
      <div class="sp-faq-list" role="list">

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-1" id="faq-q-1">
            What sizes of CMU block does AMS work with?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-1">
            <p>We work with standard 4", 6", 8", 10", and 12" CMU blocks. Block selection is determined by the structural engineer's drawings — we confirm spec before ordering.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-2" id="faq-q-2">
            Do you provide structural drawings for CMU projects?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-2">
            <p>AMS does not provide structural engineering. We work from your engineer's drawings. If you need an engineer referral, we can recommend firms we've worked with in Chicagoland.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-3" id="faq-q-3">
            What is grouting and why does it matter?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-3">
            <p>Grouting means filling CMU cells with a concrete mixture to increase structural capacity and provide a continuous mass for rebar encasement. Required cells that aren't grouted significantly reduce wall strength. Inspectors check grout placement before the wall goes higher.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-4" id="faq-q-4">
            What are control joints in CMU and where are they required?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-4">
            <p>Control joints are vertical joints filled with a flexible sealant that allow CMU walls to move with thermal expansion without cracking. IBC specifies maximum spacing — typically 25 feet. AMS installs control joints at required locations, not estimated locations.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-5" id="faq-q-5">
            Can AMS handle both interior and exterior CMU work?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-5">
            <p>Yes — interior partition walls, exterior load-bearing walls, below-grade foundations, and retaining structures. We do both standard and reinforced CMU applications.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-6" id="faq-q-6">
            Do you work directly with GCs and developers?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-6" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-6">
            <p>Yes — most of our CMU work comes through general contractors and developers. We're experienced with commercial project coordination, payment applications, and lien waivers.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-7" id="faq-q-7">
            Is AMS licensed for commercial CMU installation?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-7" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-7">
            <p>Yes — licensed in Illinois, $2.5M general liability, workers' comp on all crew. We're set up for commercial project documentation requirements.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-8" id="faq-q-8">
            What's the lead time for a commercial CMU project?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-8" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-8">
            <p>Lead time depends on block availability and crew scheduling. For large commercial projects, we recommend contacting us 4–8 weeks before your required start date.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

